<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 24551 0 R/Alt(Ten panels in five rows and two columns. Each row is one judgment (pregnancy-evidence likelihood, foreseeability, evidence relevance, negligence and suspect blame) and each column one legal context (illegal abortion, improper disposal). In each panel the horizontal axis spans the full rating scale of that judgment, the lines run over its observed ratings, and the vertical axis gives the predicted probability of finding probable cause over its full range, with one line and shaded 95% band for each outcome condition: no information, expected evidence and unexpected evidence.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[3]/Pg 77573 0 R>>
