<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 28445 0 R/Alt(Path diagram in black and white. Expected evidence and unexpected evidence, on the left and each against no information, point to pregnancy-evidence likelihood; unexpected evidence also points to foreseeability; likelihood and foreseeability point to confidence in the ruling on the right, and both kinds of evidence point directly to confidence. Each path carries its unstandardized estimate and robust Wald 95% interval, one value per legal context, tagged Abortion and Disposal; a solid path marks an interval that excludes zero and a dashed path one that includes it.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[2]/Pg 77632 0 R>>
